# Git LFS — exceptions
# The rules above match on extension alone, which catches hand-authored fixtures
# whose entire value is being readable as a diff in review. A pointer would also
# be LARGER than this file. `-filter -diff -merge` unsets the three LFS hooks;
# `text` puts it back under the `* text=auto eol=lf` rule at the top.
#
# This is not cosmetic. A path declared `filter=lfs` whose committed blob is
# plain text is reported by git-lfs on checkout as "should have been a pointer,
# but wasn't", and `git status` then calls it modified forever on any fresh
# clone — the clean filter produces a pointer that never matches the stored
# blob. A local worktree hides this behind the index stat cache, so it shows up
# only in CI, where prek stashes the phantom change, re-dirties it mid-run, and
# blames whichever hook happened to be running. Keep declaration and blob in
# agreement: either the path is excepted here, or it is `git add --renormalize`d
# into LFS.
.agents/**/tests/*.tsv -filter -diff -merge text
